#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:259
msgid "Clear formulas, fixed points, and practical advice for converting between Celsius, Fahrenheit, and Kelvin without mixing offsets and scale factors."
msgstr "Klare Formeln, Fixpunkte und praktische Ratschläge für die Umrechnung zwischen Celsius, Fahrenheit und Kelvin, ohne Offsets und Skalierungsfaktoren zu mischen."

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2259
msgid "Climb and descent rates use feet per minute—a vertical speed unit, not a horizontal airspeed unit. Do not convert fpm with knot converters."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1563
msgid "Clinic forms may ask for kilograms while your bathroom scale shows pounds, or the reverse. Convert the reading you actually measured; do not “feel” a number in the other unit. A 2–3 lb morning fluctuation is normal; a unit mix-up of 2.2× is a medical-record disaster."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:2299
msgid "Clocks label moments; durations measure spans"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:509
msgid "Clothing and body measurements often use centimetres internationally and inches in the US. Pattern drafting can mix both; convert seam allowances carefully so ease calculations stay consistent."
msgstr "Für Kleidungs- und Körpermaße werden international oft Zentimeter und in den USA Zoll verwendet. Beim Musterentwurf kann beides kombiniert werden; Konvertieren Sie die Nahtzugaben sorgfältig, damit die Berechnungen konsistent bleiben."

